Types of Frequency

1. Absolute Frequency

Absolute frequency is the total number of times a value appears in a data set.

Example

Absolute Frequency of Apple = 5

2. Relative Frequency

Relative frequency is the proportion or percentage of a value compared with the total number of observations.

Formula

Relative Frequency = Frequency / Total Number of Observations

Example

5 / 10 = 0.50 = 50%

--------------------------------------------------

Grouped Frequency Example

Score 60 - 70 : 4 students

Score 71 - 80 : 12 students

Score 81 - 90 : 8 students

Conclusion

Frequency helps us identify which values occur most often and which occur least often.

