Class Interval

A class interval is a range of values used to group similar data together, making large data sets easier to organize and understand.

--------------------------------------------------

Why Do We Use Class Intervals?

Suppose we measure the heights of 100 students.

Instead of listing every height separately, we group them into intervals.

150 - 159

160 - 169

170 - 179

This makes the data easier to read and analyze.

--------------------------------------------------

Example

Class Interval : 60 - 69
Frequency : 5

Class Interval : 70 - 79
Frequency : 12

Class Interval : 80 - 89
Frequency : 8

Class Interval : 90 - 100
Frequency : 3

--------------------------------------------------

Important Terms

Example Class Interval

70 - 79

Lower Class Limit = 70

Upper Class Limit = 79

Class Width = 10

Usually, all class intervals have the same width.

Conclusion

Class intervals simplify statistical analysis by grouping large amounts of data into meaningful ranges.

